---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = "Holy Mass & the Eucharist";
---

<Layout title={title} lang="en" plPath="/pl/eucharystia">
	<div class="eucharist-container">
		<h1>✝ Holy Mass & the Eucharist</h1>

		<p class="intro">
			The Holy Mass is the centre and summit of Christian life — the unbloody re-presentation of Christ's sacrifice on the Cross. 
			When you attend Mass, you are not going to a service. You are standing at the foot of Calvary.
		</p>

		<figure class="painting">
			<img
				src="https://archive.org/download/clevelandart-1952.112-the-mass-of-saint-gr/clevelandart-1952.112-the-mass-of-saint-gr_thumb.jpg"
				alt="The Mass of Saint Gregory — Hans Baldung (1484/85–1545)"
				loading="lazy"
				onerror="this.onerror=null;this.src='https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1952.112/1952.112_web.jpg';"
			/>
			<figcaption>
				<em>The Mass of Saint Gregory</em> — Hans Baldung Grien (c. 1511)<br />
				<small>Cleveland Museum of Art · Public Domain</small>
			</figcaption>
		</figure>

		<p class="painting-note">
			According to medieval legend, while Pope Gregory the Great was celebrating Mass, 
			Christ himself appeared to doubters — as the Man of Sorrows, rising from the altar. 
			This painting reminds us that at every Mass, He is <strong>truly present</strong> — 
			Body, Blood, Soul and Divinity.
		</p>

		<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
		<section class="section">
			<h2>🕯 How to prepare?</h2>
			<p>Arriving early — even just a few minutes — is not merely good manners. It is an act of faith. 
			The church is a place of encounter with the Living God, not an auditorium. A few pointers:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Arrive before Mass.</strong> Enter in silence, genuflect, and remind yourself where you are and before Whom you stand.</li>
				<li><strong>Examination of conscience.</strong> Is your heart ready? If you are conscious of grave sin, go to Confession first.</li>
				<li><strong>Eucharistic fast.</strong> Refrain from food and drink (except water and medicine) for one hour before Communion.</li>
				<li><strong>Prayer before Communion.</strong> You can pray traditional acts of preparation: acts of faith, hope, love and contrition.</li>
				<li><strong>Silence of soul.</strong> Turn off your phone. Leave the day's worries aside for a while. You are invited to the Lamb's banquet.</li>
			</ul>

			<div class="quote-block">
				<blockquote>
					"Be zealous in attending Holy Mass also on weekdays, even if it requires sacrifice. 
					God will reward you with his blessings and grant success in your affairs."
				</blockquote>
				<cite>— St. John Bosco</cite>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
		<section class="section">
			<h2>🔥 What do the Saints say about Holy Mass?</h2>

			<h3>On the power and mystery of Holy Mass</h3>

			<div class="quote-block">
				<blockquote>
					"It would be easier for the world to survive without the sun than to do without Holy Mass."
				</blockquote>
				<cite>— St. Padre Pio</cite>
			</div>

			<div class="quote-block">
				<blockquote>
					"If we really understood the Mass, we would die of joy."
				</blockquote>
				<cite>— St. John Mary Vianney (the Curé of Ars)</cite>
			</div>

			<div class="quote-block">
				<blockquote>
					"The celebration of Holy Mass is as valuable as the death of Jesus on the Cross."
				</blockquote>
				<cite>— St. Thomas Aquinas</cite>
			</div>

			<div class="quote-block">
				<blockquote>
					"When the Eucharist is celebrated, the sanctuary is filled with countless angels 
					who adore the Divine Victim sacrificed on the altar."
				</blockquote>
				<cite>— St. John Chrysostom</cite>
			</div>

			<h3>On receiving the Eucharist daily</h3>

			<div class="quote-block">
				<blockquote>
					"I desire the Bread of God, which is the flesh of Jesus Christ… 
					and for drink I desire his Blood, which is love incorruptible."
				</blockquote>
				<cite>— St. Ignatius of Antioch</cite>
			</div>

			<div class="quote-block">
				<blockquote>
					"Since it is the 'daily' bread, why do you take it only once a year? 
					Receive daily what is to profit you daily. Live so as to deserve to receive it daily."
				</blockquote>
				<cite>— St. Ambrose</cite>
			</div>

			<div class="quote-block">
				<blockquote>
					"You come to me and unite yourself with me intimately under the appearance of food. 
					Your Blood now flows in my veins, your Soul, O Incarnate God, penetrates mine, 
					giving me courage and support."
				</blockquote>
				<cite>— St. Maximilian Maria Kolbe</cite>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
		<section class="section faustyna">
			<h2>📖 St. Faustina Kowalska on Holy Communion</h2>
			<p class="section-intro">
				No words describe the grace of Holy Communion better than those written by the Apostle of Divine Mercy. 
				Her <em>Diary</em> is an incomparable testimony to a deep eucharistic mystical life.
			</p>

			<div class="quote-block accent">
				<span class="ref">Diary, 814</span>
				<blockquote>
					"All my strength is in You, O Living Bread. It would be very difficult for me 
					to live through the day if I did not receive Holy Communion. 
					It is my shield; without You, Jesus, I would not know how to live."
				</blockquote>
				<cite>— Drawing strength</cite>
			</div>

			<div class="quote-block accent">
				<span class="ref">Diary, 1392</span>
				<blockquote>
					"Everything that is good in me is due to Holy Communion. 
					I owe everything to it. I feel that this holy fire has transformed me completely."
				</blockquote>
				<cite>— Source of all good</cite>
			</div>

			<div class="quote-block accent">
				<span class="ref">Diary, 1037</span>
				<blockquote>
					"The only thing that keeps me alive is Holy Communion. 
					From it I draw all my strength; in it is all my power… 
					Jesus hidden in the Host is everything to me."
				</blockquote>
				<cite>— Support and consolation</cite>
			</div>

			<div class="quote-block accent">
				<span class="ref">Diary, 91</span>
				<blockquote>
					"Holy Communion assures me that I will win the victory; and so it is. 
					I fear the day on which I do not receive Holy Communion. 
					This Bread of the Strong gives me all the strength necessary to carry on my mission…"
				</blockquote>
				<cite>— Victory in daily struggles</cite>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
		<section class="section">
			<h2>🙏 How to give thanks after Communion?</h2>
			<p>
				The moments after receiving Holy Communion are the most precious prayer time of the entire day. 
				Jesus is <em>literally</em> present within you — this lasts approximately 15 minutes. 
				Do not speak. Do not reach for your phone. Remain in adoration.
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Personal thanksgiving.</strong> Tell Jesus in your own words that you love Him and what you are grateful for.</li>
				<li><strong>Intercession.</strong> There is no better moment for intercessory prayer — for family, the sick, sinners and the souls in Purgatory.</li>
				<li><strong>Act of offering.</strong> Offer Him your day, your work, your suffering — let it become an extension of His sacrifice.</li>
				<li><strong>Prayers after Communion.</strong> Traditional acts of faith, hope, love and thanksgiving (e.g. "Soul of Christ").</li>
				<li><strong>Remain in silence.</strong> Let Him speak. Often in this silence God speaks most clearly.</li>
			</ul>

			<div class="quote-block">
				<blockquote>
					"After Holy Communion, pray — not only for your own soul, but for the whole Church."
				</blockquote>
				<cite>— St. John Chrysostom</cite>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
		<section class="section closing">
			<h2>✝ The heart of it all</h2>
			<p>
				Holy Mass is not a ceremony or a spectacle. It is a Sacrifice. It is an encounter. It is a gift 
				whose value we cannot fully grasp in this life. 
				May the words of the Saints encourage you to approach the Lord's Altar 
				<strong>more often, more consciously, ever more in love with God</strong>.
			</p>
			<p class="closing-verse">
				<em>"Blessed are those who are invited to the wedding supper of the Lamb."</em><br/>
				<small>— Rev 19:9</small>
			</p>
		</section>
	</div>

	<style>
		.eucharist-container {
			max-width: 760px;
		}

		.intro {
			font-size: 1.15rem;
			line-height: 1.8;
			margin-bottom: 2rem;
			border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
			padding-left: 1rem;
		}

		/* ── Painting ── */
		.painting {
			margin: 2.5rem 0;
			text-align: center;
		}
		.painting img {
			max-width: 100%;
			width: 420px;
			border: 3px solid var(--text);
			box-shadow: 8px 8px 0 var(--text);
			display: block;
			margin: 0 auto 1rem;
		}
		.painting figcaption {
			font-size: 1rem;
			opacity: 0.75;
		}
		.painting-note {
			background: none;
			border: 2px dashed var(--text);
			padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
			font-size: 1rem;
			opacity: 0.85;
			margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
		}

		/* ── Sections ── */
		.section {
			margin-bottom: 3rem;
		}
		.section h3 {
			font-family: 'VT323', monospace;
			font-size: 1.6rem;
			color: var(--title);
			margin-top: 2rem;
			margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
		}
		.section-intro {
			opacity: 0.85;
			margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
			font-size: 1.05rem;
		}

		/* ── Quote blocks ── */
		.quote-block {
			position: relative;
			border-left: 4px solid var(--text);
			padding: 0.8rem 1.2rem;
			margin: 1.5rem 0;
			background: none;
		}
		.quote-block.accent {
			border-left-color: var(--link);
		}
		.quote-block blockquote {
			margin: 0;
			font-style: italic;
			font-size: 1.1rem;
			line-height: 1.7;
		}
		.quote-block cite {
			display: block;
			margin-top: 0.5rem;
			font-size: 0.95rem;
			opacity: 0.8;
			font-style: normal;
		}
		.quote-block .ref {
			font-family: 'VT323', monospace;
			font-size: 1rem;
			color: var(--link);
			display: block;
			margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
			opacity: 0.9;
		}

		/* ── Faustyna section ── */
		.faustyna {
			border-top: 2px solid var(--link);
			padding-top: 2rem;
		}

		/* ── Closing ── */
		.closing {
			border-top: 2px dashed var(--accent);
			padding-top: 2rem;
		}
		.closing-verse {
			text-align: center;
			font-size: 1.2rem;
			margin-top: 1.5rem;
			opacity: 0.85;
		}

		/* ── Lists ── */
		ul {
			list-style-type: square;
			padding-left: 1.2rem;
		}
		li {
			margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
			line-height: 1.6;
		}
	</style>
</Layout>
